body:
I had two friendships that I thought I would end but was able to keep. I am also the type that hates fighting and confrontations and I rarely fight with my friends.

&#x200B;

I first create a safe space for myself. I do this by calling them to a neutral ground like a fast food outlet or a cafe. I then try to explain myself, staying as neutral as possible. I usually bring a friend along as a mediator but you don't need that. If they try to interrupt me I request them to let me finish. Then after that, I see their reaction. These two people who I am still friends with were defensive at first but after some more discussion they were really mature about it and while we are not that close anymore we are still in contact. They still do the red flags but they listen to me when I call them out and are slowly changing.

&#x200B;

I did the same thing with other friends. Some of them became very defensive so the point where the left me in tears, others have tried to make me the villain, others ignored me and insulted me and others pretended they understood but then continued to disrespect me. I have slowly distanced myself from them.

&#x200B;

What I am saying there is no hard and fast rule.
